---
import BaseComponent from "../layouts/BaseComponent.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import ContactCallout from "../components/ContactCallout.astro";
import ContentCallout from "../components/ContentCallout.astro";
---

<style lang="scss">
  .get-involved-callouts {
    justify-content: center;
  }
</style>

<BaseComponent theme="theme-brown">
  <main class="get-involved-page">
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="get-involved">Get involved</h2>
      <p class="heading-text">
        Join us in building a world where everyone can be heard.
      </p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        LJN grows through collaboration, with practitioners, community members,
        partner organisations, supporters, and people who want to help reshape
        language access in meaningful ways.
      </p>
      <div class="button-wrapper">
        <Button
          href="https://forms.gle/3ZHa6ExksQKXr9bp8 "
          label="Join our network of practitioners"
        />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="why-get-involved">
        Why get involved
      </h2>
      <p class="heading-text">Why your involvement matters</p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        Language justice is collective work. It cannot be built by one
        practitioner, one organisation, or one service alone. It requires people
        willing to rethink how communication happens, support those doing the
        work, and help create systems that are safer and more inclusive.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        When you get involved with LJN, you are not only supporting one
        organisation. You are investing in a broader shift: better language
        practices, stronger multilingual leadership, more representative
        pathways into the sector, and better outcomes for communities who are
        too often expected to adapt to systems that were not built with them in
        mind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="ways-to-get-involved">
        Ways to get involved
      </h2>
      <p class="heading-text">How you can contribute</p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        Our interpreting and translation services are delivered by
        NAATI-certified practitioners who are trained in queer-affirming,
        trauma-informed, and culturally responsive practice. We support
        communication across a range of settings, including health, legal,
        migration, community, settlement, and mental health contexts.
      </p>
      <div class="content-callouts get-involved-callouts">
        <ContentCallout
          title="Partner With Us"
          body="Collaborate with LJN on training, policy development, service design, research, or community-facing projects. We work with organisations that want to improve multilingual communication in thoughtful and practical ways."
        />
        <ContentCallout
          title="Join the Lived Experience Advisory Group (LEAG)"
          body="Contribute to the development of programs, resources, and strategic priorities through lived experience leadership and community accountability."
        />
        <ContentCallout
          title="Volunteer or Mentor"
          body="Support LJN’s programs through practical contribution, mentoring, outreach, administration, or sector support. This may include supporting bilingual practitioners progressing through pathways such as Launchpad or certification programs."
        />
        <ContentCallout
          title="Work With Us"
          body="Respond to calls for interpreters, translators, project staff, trainers, and collaborators as opportunities arise. We are building a growing network of practitioners and partners aligned with LJN’s values."
        />
        <ContentCallout
          title="Donate or Fundraise"
          body="Provide financial support that helps sustain core operations, subsidise training pathways, strengthen capacity-building programs, and support community-led work."
        />
      </div>
    </section>
    <hr />
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="partnerships">Partnerships</h2>
      <p class="heading-text">Partnerships and collaboration.</p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        We collaborate with community organisations, health and legal services,
        educational institutions, funders, researchers, and practitioner
        networks. These partnerships may involve training, consulting,
        co-design, resource development, project delivery, or broader strategic
        collaboration.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        We are particularly interested in partnerships that value community
        leadership, shared learning, and long-term change. If your organisation
        is looking to strengthen language access, support multilingual
        communities more effectively, or develop safer interpreting and
        translation practices, we would love to hear from you.
      </p>
      <div class="button-wrapper">
        <Button href="mailto:admin@ljn.org.au" label="Partner with us" />
      </div>
    </section>
    <hr />
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="leag">
        LEAG / community leadership
      </h2>
      <p class="heading-text">Join the Lived Experience Advisory Group</p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        Our Lived Experience Advisory Group helps ensure that LJN’s work remains
        grounded in the realities of the communities we exist to support. LEAG
        members bring lived experience, insight, and critical perspective to the
        design of our programs, resources, and priorities.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        This is not a symbolic role. It is part of how we build accountability
        into the organisation. Members contribute to shaping training, reviewing
        resources, identifying risks and gaps, and making sure our work remains
        connected to community realities.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        If you are interested in contributing your experience, skills, or
        perspective, we would love to hear from you.
      </p>
      <div class="button-wrapper">
        <Button
          href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeoMwRuJLt33tCB1J-unr43bvOwI-1INjI9T3ZL7bB2pXf4wA/viewform?pli=1"
          label="Join the LEAG"
        />
      </div>
    </section>
    <hr />
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="volunteer-mentor">
        Volunteer / mentor
      </h2>
      <p class="heading-text">Supporting LJN beyond formal employment.</p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        There are many ways to support LJN beyond formal employment. Depending
        on your experience and capacity, involvement might include mentoring
        bilingual community members, supporting event delivery, assisting with
        communications, contributing technical or professional skills, or
        helping strengthen our operational systems.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        We value practical, thoughtful contributions and are especially
        interested in people who want to work in ways that are collaborative,
        community-aware, and values-aligned.
      </p>
      <div class="button-wrapper">
        <Button
          href="https://forms.gle/yvgWwrsZPxTjRyeM6 "
          label="Volunteer with us"
        />
      </div>
    </section>
    <hr />
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="eyebrow-text sidebar-entry" id="donate">Donate</h2>
      <p class="heading-text">Support language justice.</p>
      <p class="intro-text">
        Donations help LJN build the infrastructure and programs needed for
        long-term change. This includes supporting bilingual LGBTQIA+ people
        through training and certification pathways, developing community-led
        resources, sustaining workshops and forums, and strengthening the
        operational foundations that allow the organisation to grow responsibly.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        Every contribution supports more than a service. It supports a future
        where multilingual communication is safer, more representative, and more
        accountable.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">Send us an email if you'd like to donate to us!</p>
      <div class="button-wrapper">
        <Button href="mailto:admin@ljn.org.au" label="Donate now" />
      </div>
    </section>
    <hr />
    <ContactCallout />
  </main>
</BaseComponent>
